1
00:00:01,459 --> 00:00:03,128
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:09,259
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:10,802
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:16,224
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,226
[Jesabel] I checked all the yachts.

7
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:20,186
I didn’t see Grey Shadow.

8
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,730
What could Grey Shadow mean?

9
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,231
Missing cat?!

10
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:24,607
His name is Tamago.

11
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:27,485
[Helper] We’ll go ahead,
since it seems you can’t find him.

12
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:29,112
This is cat fur.

13
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:30,905
The cat is so cute, Sir.

14
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:31,740
[Ashley] Frankie?

15
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:32,991
I wanted to take him.

16
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:34,409
[music intensifies]

17
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,036
[Atoy] He knows us.

18
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,954
Hey, your owner is looking for you.

19
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,539
Go back to your owner, Frankie.

20
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:41,541
Frank Cohen was the name Samir used.

21
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:42,459
Where’s Gavin?

22
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:43,626
[Audrey] Why?

23
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,628
[Cita] Nothing,
I just wanted to know their whereabouts.

24
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:48,381
You know,
I don’t want Karla to have a baby yet.

25
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:50,216
[Gavin] Let’s stay here.

26
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:50,800
Just 5 seconds.

27
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:52,385
[music continues]

28
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:53,636
What are you doing?!

29
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,889
[music continues]

30
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:57,640
There are so many of you,
you’re all handsome.

31
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,851
One even looks like Atoy.

32
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:01,311
[music continues]

33
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:02,062
Why are you together?

34
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:02,645
[cat-calling sound] Psst, psst.

35
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:04,314
- Hey, hey, hey, hey.
- Whoa!

36
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:05,440
That’s it, that’s it.

37
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:06,983
Maybe you saw him.

38
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,401
Look, it’s Tamago.

39
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:09,861
That’s the one we saw earlier.

40
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:11,029
Yes, we saw him earlier.

41
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:11,988
- You saw him?!
- [Both] Yes.

42
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:12,572
He looked like that, right?

43
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:14,115
Yes, but now his name is Frankie.

44
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,325
[Atoy]  I have an idea.

45
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:16,576
Jump into the water.

46
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:18,745
- [water splashes]
- [Jesabel] Maybe you have extra clothes,

47
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:20,497
because I’m cold.

48
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,581
[grunts & groans]

49
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:23,083
[thumps] That’s what I’m telling you.

50
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:24,626
[Atoy]  Which one of you is Eman?

51
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:25,919
I’m Alvin’s cousin, he sent me.

52
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:27,420
Boss Artem already went ahead.

53
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:28,963
[Eman] Come on, get in.

54
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:31,090
We still can’t find the cat.

55
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:33,259
[Emerson] Maybe you can help me.

56
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:35,053
[Atoy] Ask Jesabel for help, she’s there.

57
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:36,262
You-- you jump, I jump!

58
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:37,514
[cat yowls & gasps] [squeals]

59
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,098
Oh! Yes! Yes!

60
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:40,308
[Eman] We’re here!

61
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:42,560
Come on! Move, we have a lot of work!

62
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:43,978
Don’t be stupid!

63
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,188
Especially you, Ronald!

64
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:46,856
[music swells]

65
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:53,738
[tense music playing]

66
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:03,665
[music fades]

67
00:02:03,748 --> 00:02:05,333
[Atoy]  What is this doing here?

68
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:07,585
[theme music playing]

69
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:11,047
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪

70
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:16,052
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

71
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,221
♪ Wait a moment, Mister Tailor ♪

72
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:19,556
♪ Can you sew ♪

73
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:20,932
♪ The hole in my polo

74
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:23,351
that’s right under the armpit ♪

75
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:25,937
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

76
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:27,522
♪ There’s a secret behind ♪

77
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:29,440
♪ If your measurement is wrong ♪

78
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:33,570
♪ The whole movement turns crooked… ♪

79
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:34,696
[gunshots]

80
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:36,447
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

81
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:39,325
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

82
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,410
[music swells]

83
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:44,247
[music fades]

84
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:48,209
[waves crashing]

85
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,421
- [fizz of radio static]
- Sir, we’re here at the main deck.

86
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:54,215
[Artem on the radio]
You can go down here, now.

87
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,384
Copy, Sir.

88
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:57,635
Let’s go.

89
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,846
[suspicious music playing]

90
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:19,824
It stinks!

91
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:21,701
[Transporter 3]
Those fish are probably decaying!

92
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:23,995
[music swells]

93
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:25,455
[music fades]

94
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:47,936
Ah, we were just playing.

95
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:50,647
Playing? What kind of game is this,

96
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,106
that you need to cover her mouth?

97
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:54,317
We were playing charades,

98
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,485
- Miss Cita.
- Mmm-mmm.

99
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:58,112
Then Ibyang and I were guessing

100
00:03:58,196 --> 00:03:59,447
what they were acting out.

101
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:01,449
[Gavin] Right?

102
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:02,784
They’re lying!

103
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:04,327
When we entered the room,

104
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:07,872
we saw them lying on top
of each other on the floor!

105
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,290
[Both]  What?!

106
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,959
[pleasant music playing]

107
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:14,671
Ibyang, is your sister telling the truth?

108
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:16,172
Yes, Mama.

109
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:18,424
[music continues]

110
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:24,555
Gavin… you have some explaining to do.

111
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:26,224
Karla.

112
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:29,727
[music fades]

113
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:35,024
[mysterious music playing]

114
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,952
[Atoy]  Son of a thread.

115
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:48,162
So, this is where they’re hiding them.

116
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:49,539
You’re late.

117
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:50,915
Sorry, Sir.

118
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:51,958
[music continues]

119
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:56,921
Is this everything?

120
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:58,214
Yes, Sir.

121
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:01,843
Okay. Gentlemen, you have one job today,

122
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:05,054
and it is to bring
these crates to the yacht.

123
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:10,018
But remember,
one scratch on any of these crates,

124
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,729
and you will not be paid.

125
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:14,272
You understand?

126
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:15,398
[Transporters] Yes, Sir!

127
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:17,317
You will wait for Artem on the yacht,

128
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:22,071
and do not open these crates.

129
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,072
Go.

130
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:28,369
[suspicious music playing]

131
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:52,977
What’s inside these crates?

132
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:54,562
They’re so heavy!

133
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,064
Don’t ask.

134
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:57,440
Just work!

135
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,318
[music continues]

136
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:02,487
You, you look strong.

137
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:04,864
You carry these up the stairs.

138
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:06,949
We’ll go back for the others.

139
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:11,370
[sneaky music playing]

140
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,039
You can handle it.

141
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:14,665
[music continues]

142
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,464
[device blips]

143
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:44,862
[music swells]

144
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:47,532
[suspicious music playing]

145
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:50,743
[Atoy]
What will they use all this gold for?

146
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:56,791
[music continues]

147
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,172
[music swells]

148
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:09,846
[Artem] So…

149
00:07:10,888 --> 00:07:11,764
[music fades]

150
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,975
where are we going to place all the gold?

151
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:15,268
In the office.

152
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:21,441
[ominous music playing]

153
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:24,402
But only for a short time,

154
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:26,946
we have to exchange it for cash.

155
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:29,031
We have a lot to prepare

156
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:31,033
and people to pay

157
00:07:31,117 --> 00:07:32,076
to make the Big Bang happen.

158
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:36,038
[Atoy]  Prepare? Big Bang?

159
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:44,672
[tense music playing]

160
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:48,050
[ominous music playing]

161
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:49,677
Hey!

162
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,179
What are you doing here?

163
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:52,930
[suspenseful music playing]

164
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:54,015
Sir, I uh…

165
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:54,807
I’ll get the crate.

166
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:57,143
Go back.

167
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,812
Only 4 crates to transport.

168
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:00,730
You wait for me there.

169
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:02,523
Okay, Sir. Sorry.

170
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:03,941
[music fades]

171
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,359
[tense music playing]

172
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:09,030
[music fades]

173
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:19,624
But it was really just an accident.

174
00:08:20,625 --> 00:08:21,709
I was fixing the curtain,

175
00:08:21,792 --> 00:08:23,544
then I lost my balance on the table.

176
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:25,713
Gavin caught me, that’s all that happened.

177
00:08:25,796 --> 00:08:28,466
Then why did you have to lie, huh?

178
00:08:28,549 --> 00:08:31,010
Eh, eh--eh, because--

179
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:32,386
Because you’d get mad.

180
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:34,555
Of course we’d get mad!

181
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:35,181
Didn’t we tell you

182
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:38,267
to keep your distance from each other?!

183
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:39,143
You didn’t listen!

184
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,270
What if we weren’t here?

185
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:42,396
What if--

186
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,273
What if you were already undressing?!

187
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:45,983
Mom, gosh!

188
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,486
I’m not that kind of girl.

189
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:50,988
[Karla] I know what’s right and wrong.

190
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,907
And I still have so many things

191
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,283
I want to do in my life.

192
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:56,953
I, myself, know that I shouldn't,
you know, get pregnant.

193
00:08:57,036 --> 00:08:59,205
It wouldn’t reach that point.

194
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:01,457
You’re just saying that now,

195
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:03,709
but when you’re in the situation--

196
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:05,211
Oh my.

197
00:09:05,294 --> 00:09:06,963
I’m just not comfortable about this.

198
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,714
I’ll tell Atoy when he gets back.

199
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,175
Mom, does Big Brother Atoy
really need to know?

200
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,969
It was really just an accident.

201
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:14,720
Ah, enough.

202
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:16,931
This meeting is over.

203
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:23,938
[pensive music playing]

204
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:26,065
Eh-- Gavin, wait.

205
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:28,693
Gavin!

206
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:39,036
[music fades]

207
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:44,333
[suspicious music playing]

208
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:03,352
There’s someone here.

209
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:24,790
[music fades] Son of a--

210
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,000
Why are you here?!

211
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,711
Sir, sorry. I uh…

212
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,296
I just went to pee.

213
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,048
If we get in trouble for this,

214
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:33,716
I’ll take all your salary, okay.

215
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,176
Come on.

216
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:40,389
[heavy music playing]

217
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:53,944
Who are you? What are you doing here?

218
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,029
[mutters]

219
00:10:55,112 --> 00:10:59,533
[music continues]

220
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:00,826
[Alvin] Hurry up.

221
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:05,081
[music continues]

222
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:06,540
Tie his feet.

223
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:11,587
[music continues]

224
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:19,720
- Lend me your phone.
- I said I’ll borrow it.

225
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,097
[grunts]

226
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,223
[thumps]

227
00:11:22,306 --> 00:11:26,018
[foreboding music playing]

228
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:37,071
[phone clicking]

229
00:11:37,154 --> 00:11:39,532
[line rings]

230
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:42,785
[phone ringing]

231
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:45,955
[music continues]

232
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:46,580
Who is this?

233
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:48,124
Hello! This is Alvin!

234
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:50,126
I am one of the transporters!

235
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:51,961
Someone knocked me out…

236
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:53,963
[Alvin on the phone]
on the way to the yacht!

237
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,256
He could be a policeman

238
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:57,007
pretending to be a transporter!

239
00:11:58,592 --> 00:11:59,885
Please be on alert!

240
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:00,845
[music fades]

241
00:12:00,928 --> 00:12:01,429
[tense music playing]

242
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,596
Samir!

243
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,597
[music continues]

244
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:05,975
One of the transporters is an intruder!

245
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:11,772
[music swells]

246
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:15,317
Gavin, why are you leaving?

247
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,237
No one is asking you to leave.

248
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:20,114
Don’t worry.

249
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,532
I’ll talk to Miss Cita, okay?

250
00:12:21,615 --> 00:12:22,408
Mmm, Auntie, Auntie!

251
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,617
Please don’t, please don’t.

252
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:27,496
Ah, I don’t want
to impose myself here anymore.

253
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,915
Besides, this is your family.

254
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,168
What are you talking about?

255
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:35,212
You are family.

256
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,382
You’re my favorite nephew, right?

257
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:40,009
Aunt, you don’t have a choice.

258
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:41,427
I’m your only nephew.

259
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:43,179
Even so.

260
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:44,763
But I’ve made my decision.

261
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:47,933
I'll just be the one to stay away so…

262
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:50,811
Miss Cita won't get stressed,
and neither will you.

263
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:53,647
Where are you going?

264
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:55,900
I’ll rent a condo.

265
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:57,735
There’s one near our school.

266
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:58,736
I’ll just let you know.

267
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:01,530
But that’s far from here.

268
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:04,700
I want you to stay near me, Gavin.

269
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,410
Look.

270
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:08,579
I know that you’re already an adult,

271
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,749
but you still need
to be around a real adult.

272
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:13,792
[Audrey]  You know what I mean?

273
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,252
I know. I know, Auntie.

274
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:18,422
I’ll also tell Brother Atoy, okay?

275
00:13:31,101 --> 00:13:31,936
[Audrey]  Be good, ah.

276
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:33,562
Yeah.

277
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:36,023
[music fades]

278
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:37,525
[waves crashing]

279
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,526
Move quickly!

280
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,448
[ominous music playing]

281
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:47,535
Nobody leaves until I say so.

282
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:52,081
[music continues]

283
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:53,999
Sir, what did we do?

284
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,586
I thought we had an agreement, gentlemen.

285
00:13:58,629 --> 00:14:00,548
The crates are safe and protected.

286
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:02,800
[music continues]

287
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:05,219
There seems to be a shark here

288
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:06,720
in a dolphin suit.

289
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:08,138
[music continues]

290
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:11,016
And I will find out who that is.

291
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,102
[music swells]

292
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:14,812
Remove your masks.

293
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:17,940
[tense music playing]

294
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:27,908
[music fades]

295
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:29,451
[thumps]

296
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:30,578
[bullet whizzes]

297
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:32,037
[thumps]

298
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,914
[bullets whizzing]

299
00:14:33,998 --> 00:14:34,790
Sir, Sir, don’t, don’t--

300
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:35,624
[bullet whizzes]

301
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:36,667
[music continues]

302
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,168
[bullets whizzing]

303
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:39,211
[thuds]

304
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:41,297
[thumps]

305
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,549
[music continues]

306
00:14:43,632 --> 00:14:46,010
[bullets whizzing]

307
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:50,306
[music continues]

308
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:52,016
[bullets whizzing]

309
00:14:52,099 --> 00:14:55,102
[music continues]

310
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:58,814
[gate lock clanging]

311
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:05,112
[music continues]

312
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:05,738
[bullet whizzes]

313
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:12,286
[music continues]

314
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,714
[bullet whizzes]

315
00:15:23,797 --> 00:15:24,423
[action music playing]

316
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:25,049
[bullets whizzing]

317
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:28,052
[music continues]
[gun cocking]

318
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:29,678
[gate lock clangs]

319
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:38,228
[music fades]

320
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,147
[footsteps tapping]

321
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:42,274
Who-- who are you?

322
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:44,151
What are you doing here?

323
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:46,445
[tense music playing]

324
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:47,404
Oka?

325
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:50,115
[music continues]

326
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,200
[gate lock clanging]

327
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:58,707
[music swells]

328
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:03,462
[music intensifies]

329
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:07,299
[tense music playing]

330
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,843
[bullets whizzing]

331
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:13,472
[music fades]

332
00:16:13,555 --> 00:16:14,807
I know you were here.

333
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:18,310
[ominous music playing]

334
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:20,479
I know you’re here.

335
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,522
You are an imposter!

336
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:23,065
[music fades]

337
00:16:24,149 --> 00:16:25,609
[Atoy]  I’m not that stupid, Samir.

338
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:29,279
[rousing music playing]

339
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:33,450
It sounds like
your real voice is coming out.

340
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:34,952
[clangs, then clatters]

341
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:35,995
[groans]

342
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:42,209
[ominous music playing]

343
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,879
I knew it was you.

344
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:46,839
I hate to say this,

345
00:16:46,922 --> 00:16:49,508
but I am impressed, Atoy.

346
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:50,884
So, you are impressed.

347
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:53,721
I will be more impressed

348
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:56,306
if you tell me
where the other trackers are.

349
00:16:57,766 --> 00:16:59,101
Where did you bring my boss?

350
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,395
What did you do to him?!

351
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:04,023
- Business.
- [Atoy] Business?

352
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:08,527
Is that your business? To kill people?

353
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:11,613
You’re monsters, you terrorists.

354
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:16,785
Now maybe it’s time
you join your own boss.

355
00:17:16,869 --> 00:17:17,870
[swishes & clangs]

356
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:19,621
[action music playing]

357
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:23,542
[swishing & clanging]

358
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:25,919
[thumping & thudding]

359
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:27,296
[grunts & groans]

360
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:28,714
[thumps]

361
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:31,759
[swishes, thumps & clangs]

362
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:38,348
[swishing, thumping, and clanging]

363
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:44,396
[Ibyang] Is this Tatoy?

364
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:47,608
Ah, he looks chubby!

365
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:49,359
- Hmm.
- So that’s why, it seems…

366
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,320
he’s often in the kitchen.

367
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:53,155
Hmm, right?

368
00:17:53,238 --> 00:17:54,448
Maybe…

369
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,201
- they always have delicious food.
- Mmm-mmm, true.

370
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,827
[chuckles]

371
00:17:59,953 --> 00:18:01,497
So cute!

372
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:02,456
[light music playing]

373
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:03,040
Oh.

374
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:04,458
What is it?

375
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:08,921
[pensive music playing]

376
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:13,759
[Ibyang] Uhm…

377
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:16,136
Tatoy is really handsome!

378
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:18,639
[Janine] But wait.

379
00:18:19,306 --> 00:18:20,724
Who’s with him, Mommy?

380
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:22,434
It looks like…

381
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:24,269
they’re best friends.

382
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,688
Eh, I don’t know him.

383
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:29,358
If Daddy Tatoy did mention him,

384
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:31,693
I don’t remember.

385
00:18:31,777 --> 00:18:34,988
Where could Tatoy’s best friend be?

386
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:37,282
[rousing music playing]

387
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:40,452
[thumping & thudding]

388
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:42,079
[grunting & groaning]

389
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:44,540
[rock music playing]

390
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,421
[thumps & clangs]

391
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:58,053
[music swells]

392
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:01,140
[bullets whizzing]

393
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,599
[tense music playing]

394
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:06,812
[explosions & rumbling]

395
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:10,566
[fire crackling]

396
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:11,275
[heavy music playing]

397
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,401
We have to go now!

398
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,403
[explosion & rumbles nearby]

399
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:15,821
Sir, what about the gold?!

400
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:17,990
Leave the gold! The ship is going down!

401
00:19:18,073 --> 00:19:19,158
[grunts]

402
00:19:19,241 --> 00:19:20,868
[music continues]

403
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:25,497
[electricity & fire crackling]

404
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,291
Atoy, Atoy.

405
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,168
Psst, hey.

406
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:33,839
[electricity and fire crackling]

407
00:19:33,922 --> 00:19:38,552
I knew it, you were the one I saw earlier.

408
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:39,469
Oka?

409
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:40,971
This ship is sinking,

410
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:42,389
we need to leave now.

411
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:44,808
[electricity & fire crackling]

412
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,101
Son of a thread.

413
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,728
[electricity & fire crackling]

414
00:19:47,811 --> 00:19:48,353
Okay.

415
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:49,938
[electricity & fire crackling]

416
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:51,231
[suspenseful music playing]

417
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:54,401
[explosions & rumbling]

418
00:19:54,484 --> 00:19:58,071
[music intensifies]

419
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:00,407
[water swashing]

420
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:07,164
[music continues]

421
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:33,232
[explosions & rumbling]

422
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,902
[music intensifies]

423
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:45,994
This is a big, big problem.

424
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:48,872
None of this would have happened

425
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:51,250
if not for Atoy Padua!

426
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:56,129
- Atoy?
- Yes.

427
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:58,298
He was there.

428
00:20:59,007 --> 00:21:00,217
He was the intruder!

429
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:02,928
It’s a good thing he’s dead now.

430
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:04,846
[suspicious music playing]

431
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:07,724
Atoy is very slippery.

432
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:10,727
He cheated death many, many times.

433
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:12,938
And I will not stop

434
00:21:13,021 --> 00:21:18,110
until I see
his rotten corpse in the grave.

435
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:22,614
[music swells]

436
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:26,451
[waves crashing & rumbling]

437
00:21:31,748 --> 00:21:34,584
[water swashing]

438
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:39,506
[tense music playing]

439
00:21:40,048 --> 00:21:45,679
[water bubbling]

440
00:21:45,762 --> 00:21:49,850
[music continues]

441
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:52,185
[music swells]

442
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:53,645
Oka!

443
00:21:54,646 --> 00:22:00,902
- [music fades]
- [electronic blipping]

444
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:02,904
[intense music playing]

445
00:22:05,407 --> 00:22:06,575
[Coastguard] Come with me first.

446
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:07,659
There was an unusual explosion

447
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:08,327
in the middle of the sea.

448
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,120
That was Samir and his men.

449
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:11,496
Oh no, where are the others?

450
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:12,205
[theme music playing]

451
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:15,000
[water splashes]
[grunting & growling]

452
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:16,376
[thumping]

453
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:17,794
- Oscar is alive.
- You see?

454
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:20,505
If he can survive an explosion,

455
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:21,673
what about Atoy?

456
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,885
[Samir] He cheated death many times.

457
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:27,137
And I will not stop

458
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:30,766
until I see his corpse in the grave.

459
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:31,808
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

460
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:32,768
[Atoy] Oka!

461
00:22:33,351 --> 00:22:34,186
We’re already at the hospital.

462
00:22:34,269 --> 00:22:36,813
[music swells]

463
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:41,401
Rachel C. Arias: Script Producer
